Detailed Challenges\par
\par
Grid Integration & Intermittency: Both solar and wind suffer from variability. Without scalable battery storage (like Li-ion or flow batteries) or green hydrogen backup, sudden weather changes can destabilize grid frequency.\par
\par
Supply Chain & Recycling: Solar panels and wind turbine blades face end-of-life disposal challenges. Processing solar materials requires mining heavy metals and silicon, while older composite turbine blades often end up in landfills.\par
\par
Geographical Constraints: Geothermal requires high subsurface heat profiles (mostly near tectonic boundaries), and large-scale hydro requires suitable river topographies, limiting widespread deployment compared to solar or wind.\par
