  during combustion.\par
\par
Ocean Energy (Tidal & Wave Power): Harnesses the kinetic energy of ocean tides, currents, or surface waves using underwater turbines or floating ocean devices.\par
\par
Advantage: Highly predictable (tides follow precise astronomical cycles, unlike wind or sun).\par
\par
Drawback: Harsh saltwater environments cause rapid corrosion and high equipment maintenance costs.\par
\par
Green Hydrogen: Formed by using renewable power (like solar or wind) to split water into hydrogen and oxygen via electrolysis. While technically an energy carrier rather than a primary natural resource, it functions as a primary clean fuel alternative.  \par
