 : Produces no air pollutants or carbon during power generation.\par
\par
Small Land Footprint: Requires significantly less land area per megawatt compared to solar or wind farms.\par
\par
Cons:\par
\par
Radioactive Waste: Produces spent fuel that remains hazardous for thousands of years and requires long-term geologic storage.\par
\par
High Upfront Costs: Construction of traditional large reactors takes years to decades and carries massive capital requirements.\par
\par
Safety & Proliferation Concerns: Severe accident risks (e.g., Chernobyl, Fukushima) and potential proliferation risks require stringent safety standards.\par
